But the convergence of two opposed observers on the same diagnosis points past this one event.
As the disciplining structures of organized extremism thin, the violence they once shaped does not disappear; it disperses into a culture that supplies an endless stockpile of grievance, aesthetics, and martyrs to remix.
The work ahead is less about decoding a coherent enemy than about recognizing how little coherence the next attack might need.
